# API Development

- Expense REST API uses Flask in `API/` (do not add another framework).
- Validate required request fields in the API layer before calling Models.
- Prefer small private helpers over new validation frameworks or dependencies.
- Handle malformed or missing JSON at the API boundary and return consistent JSON 400 responses.
- Keep success/error JSON shapes consistent (`status`, `message`).
- Do not write to real MongoDB during verification unless the user explicitly approves.
- Prefer Flask test client + mocks for API checks when safe.
- Keep changes scoped to the requested API task; do not modify Models unless required.
